WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.007
How can one number have several correct
representations?

2
00:00:03.506 --> 00:00:06.142
We can write its digits, say it in words,
or

3
00:00:06.211 --> 00:00:07.709
split it into place values.

4
00:00:08.162 --> 00:00:10.228
All three describe the same quantity.

5
00:00:10.762 --> 00:00:13.990
Let us represent four hundred and six
thousand, two hundred

6
00:00:14.025 --> 00:00:17.520
and seventy five. Start with the largest
place.

7
00:00:17.787 --> 00:00:20.039
The four means four hundred thousand.

8
00:00:20.329 --> 00:00:22.860
The zero ten thousands contributes zero.

9
00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:25.519
The six means six thousand.

10
00:00:26.175 --> 00:00:29.356
Keep that zero as a placeholder when
writing the standard

11
00:00:29.414 --> 00:00:32.967
number, so every other digit stays in the
right place.

12
00:00:33.617 --> 00:00:38.006
Now add the smaller places: two hundred,
seventy and five.

13
00:00:38.493 --> 00:00:42.498
The expanded form is four hundred
thousand, plus six thousand,

14
00:00:42.789 --> 00:00:45.610
plus two hundred, plus seventy, plus five.

15
00:00:46.121 --> 00:00:49.104
We can leave out the zero contribution
without changing the

16
00:00:49.162 --> 00:00:53.769
total. In words, say four hundred and six
thousand, two

17
00:00:53.839 --> 00:00:55.046
hundred and seventy five.

18
00:00:55.418 --> 00:00:58.250
Notice how the thousands group and the
final three digits

19
00:00:58.308 --> 00:01:02.871
fit together. The word form, standard form
and expanded form

20
00:01:03.115 --> 00:01:06.876
all represent four hundred and six
thousand, two hundred and

21
00:01:06.934 --> 00:01:09.721
seventy five. We can also regroup a
number.

22
00:01:10.116 --> 00:01:13.192
Three thousand four hundred is three
thousands and four hundreds.

23
00:01:13.666 --> 00:01:17.393
It is also thirty four hundreds, because
thirty four groups

24
00:01:17.439 --> 00:01:20.493
of one hundred make three thousand four
hundred.

25
00:01:20.911 --> 00:01:23.302
The grouping changes; the amount does not.

26
00:01:23.743 --> 00:01:28.341
For practice, combine six hundred
thousand, twenty thousand, four

27
00:01:28.411 --> 00:01:30.199
thousand, three hundred and eight.

28
00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:33.937
That gives six hundred and twenty four
thousand, three hundred

29
00:01:33.972 --> 00:01:37.060
and eight. There are no tens, but the zero
still

30
00:01:37.118 --> 00:01:41.629
holds their place. Remember: read,
partition and regroup, while keeping

31
00:01:41.675 --> 00:01:42.790
the value unchanged.

